{"step_index":437,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T12:52:27Z","content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. It should be noted that 109.62.64.18:9443 redirects to Map [172.30.198.50].\n2. [root@th2-centprop-be1 ~]# ip route show\ndefault via 172.30.198.54 dev ens192 proto static metric 100 \n172.30.198.48/29 dev ens192 proto kernel scope link src 172.30.198.49 metric 100 \n[root@th2-centprop-be1 ~]# ip route add 109.62.64.18/32 via 172.30.198.33\nError: Nexthop has invalid gateway.\n3. The external user connects to the url extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr on 443 which is the Centreon Web UI. Then he connects to the Map server using the Map option [/home/koby/Pictures/Screenshots/Screenshot From 2026-09-10 15-56-25.png].\n4. Give all the configurations that need to done on the backend and reverse proxy!\n5. Please check the nginx config on the reverse proxy and modify it if required.\n6. I also added lo-alias interface!\n7. [root@th2-centprop-be1 ~]# cat /etc/hosts\n127.0.0.1   localhost localhost.localdomain localhost4 localhost4.localdomain4\n::1         localhost localhost.localdomain localhost6 localhost6.localdomain6\n#127.0.1.1   th2-centprop-be1.infra.intranet.local  th2-centprop-be1\n172.30.198.49    th2-centprop-be1.infra.intranet.local    th2-centprop-be1\n172.30.198.57    th2-centprop-db1.infra.intranet.local    th2-centprop-db1\n172.30.166.49   mau-centprop-pol1.infra.intranet.local  mau-centprop-pol1\n172.30.38.49    mtq-centprop-pol1.infra.intranet.local  mtq-centprop-pol1\n#127.0.0.1 extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\n#172.30.198.33 extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\n172.30.198.33 map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\n8. I did the test but failed. /home/koby/Pictures/Screenshots/Screenshot From 2026-09-10 16-39-40.png\n/home/koby/Pictures/Screenshots/Screenshot From 2026-09-10 16-40-10.png\n9. Please stop h\n<truncated 5320 bytes>\n.30.198.33:9443/` $\\rightarrow$ `301` to `/centreon-map/`.\n  * `https://172.30.198.33:9443/centreon-map/` $\\rightarrow$ `401 Unauthorized` (Centreon Map API response).\n  * `https://extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:443/` $\\rightarrow$ `301` to `/centreon/` $\\rightarrow$ Centreon Web.\n* **External Client Flow**:\n  * External Client $\\rightarrow$ Public DNS (`109.62.64.18:9443`) $\\rightarrow$ Firewall DNAT $\\rightarrow$ Reverse Proxy (`172.30.198.33:9443`) $\\rightarrow$ Map (`172.30.198.50:9443`). Operational (requires certificate acceptance in browser).\n* **Backend Flow**:\n  * Central `.49` $\\rightarrow$ `/etc/hosts` $\\rightarrow$ Reverse Proxy `172.30.198.33:9443` $\\rightarrow$ Map `172.30.198.50:9443`. Operational at network layer; blocked in UI test button solely by SSL cert validation.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Next Steps\n\n1. **Expand Let's Encrypt Certificate**:\n   * Add `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` to the Certbot certificate on `172.30.198.33`:\n     ```bash\n     sudo certbot --expand -d extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr,map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\n     ```\n     *(Or via DNS-01 challenge using `~/.ansible/playbooks/issue-deploy-certs.yml`).*\n2. **Reload Nginx**:\n   * Once renewed, run `sudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx`.\n3. **Retest UI Button**:\n   * Re-run `[Test connection to server]` in Centreon Web (`Administration > Extensions > Options`). With a matching SAN in the certificate, PHP cURL will validate the TLS handshake and show a green success mark.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n* All background tasks have been terminated (`manage_task` kill); no lingering background processes exist.\n* Strict caution: avoid running intrusive background tests or modifying unrelated firewa